# Template for the untracked `local.properties` (PLAT-06 / D-08).
#
# Copy the keys below into your own `local.properties` (which is gitignored) and replace
# every REPLACE_ME value, or set the SAME-NAMED environment variables in CI. An
# environment variable wins over a `local.properties` entry for the same key.
#
# These are NOT cryptographic secrets — they ship inside the APK and anyone can read them
# out of a published build. They are kept out of version control for a different reason:
# a committed ID lets a forked repo serve ads against this AdMob account, and invalid
# traffic gets an AdMob account suspended non-appealably.
#
# A DEBUG BUILD NEEDS NONE OF THIS. `assembleDebug`, `check`, `test` and Android Studio
# sync all work on a fresh clone with this file never copied — the three AD units are
# hard-wired on debug to Google's published test units, and a value set below is ignored
# for them (see build-logic/src/main/kotlin/AdIdDefaults.kt). PGS_PROJECT_ID is the one
# exception — a project ID cannot serve an ad, so debug honours it; see its key comment.
# Only a release invocation (`assembleRelease`, `bundleRelease`, or a bare `assemble` /
# `build` / `bundle`, which build both variants) requires real values; it fails at
# configuration time with a message naming the exact key that is missing.
#
# A value that is absent, blank, or still prefixed `REPLACE_ME` all count as "not set".

# AdMob application ID — the `ca-app-pub-…~…` form (tilde, not slash).
ADMOB_APP_ID=REPLACE_ME_ADMOB_APP_ID

# Rewarded ad unit — the hint / undo / retry surface.
ADMOB_REWARDED_AD_UNIT_ID=REPLACE_ME_ADMOB_REWARDED_AD_UNIT_ID

# Interstitial ad unit — the between-levels surface.
ADMOB_INTERSTITIAL_AD_UNIT_ID=REPLACE_ME_ADMOB_INTERSTITIAL_AD_UNIT_ID

# Play Games Services project ID from the Play Console (numeric).
# Unlike the three AdMob keys above, a DEBUG build HONOURS this value: set it and your
# debug builds sign in to the REAL Play Games project (that is what the debug-keystore
# SHA-1 is registered for). Leave it unset or `REPLACE_ME` and debug falls back to the
# inert "0" placeholder, where Play Games sign-in will simply never succeed.
PGS_PROJECT_ID=REPLACE_ME_PGS_PROJECT_ID

# =============================================================================
# Play Games leaderboard and achievement IDs (27 keys — D-17 / PLAT-06)
# =============================================================================
#
# These come from the Play Console once the leaderboards and achievements actually exist
# (Phase 14 / the 12-08 operator checklist). Until that project is created there is
# nothing to paste here, and that is fine — see the next paragraph.
#
# A DEBUG BUILD NEEDS NONE OF THEM. An unset key resolves to `UNCONFIGURED-<KEY>`, which
# is a real, well-formed string the Play Games SDK simply rejects server-side. The game
# builds, the whole JVM suite runs, and only submission is inert. A RELEASE invocation
# behaves the opposite way: it fails at configuration time with a message naming every
# missing key, and a copy-pasted `UNCONFIGURED-…` value counts as missing too.
#
# Unlike the AdMob block above, the ads suspension paragraph does NOT apply here — that
# risk is about serving real ads from a development device and has no Play Games
# equivalent. Debug therefore HONOURS a value set below, deliberately: Google publishes no
# test leaderboard/achievement IDs, and the Play Games project registers the debug-keystore
# SHA-1 precisely so debug builds can sign in and submit. Be aware of the flip side: fill
# in real IDs here and your debug builds write to the REAL leaderboards.
#
# These are not secrets either — they ship inside the APK. They stay out of git so a fork
# cannot write to this game's leaderboards and achievements.

# --- Play Games leaderboard IDs (7) ------------------------------------------

# Challenge ladder — highest Challenge level reached (PGSL-01).
PGS_LB_CHALLENGE_LADDER=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CHALLENGE_LADDER

# Challenge cumulative score — SUM(bestScore) over solved Challenge levels (PGSL-02).
PGS_LB_CHALLENGE_SCORE=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CHALLENGE_SCORE

# Classic board leaderboard — English-33.
PGS_LB_CLASSIC_ENGLISH33=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CLASSIC_ENGLISH33

# Classic board leaderboard — European-37.
PGS_LB_CLASSIC_EUROPEAN37=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CLASSIC_EUROPEAN37

# Classic board leaderboard — Asymmetric-39.
PGS_LB_CLASSIC_ASYMMETRIC39=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CLASSIC_ASYMMETRIC39

# Classic board leaderboard — Diamond-41.
PGS_LB_CLASSIC_DIAMOND41=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CLASSIC_DIAMOND41

# Classic board leaderboard — Wiegleb-45.
PGS_LB_CLASSIC_WIEGLEB45=REPLACE_ME_PGS_LB_CLASSIC_WIEGLEB45

